/-!
# Geometric Satake and fusion, part II: target signatures

The roadmap is README.md; this file is not the roadmap. This acceptance file records
which of the roadmap's headline theorems can be stated against the pinned APIs.
None of the following geometric headlines is statable at these pins:

* Polynomial local-model normality and adjoint/derived-isogeny comparison (Layer 1)
  lack polynomial Beilinson–Drinfeld Grassmannians and their schematic Schubert closures.
* Auxiliary prime-to-p Hodge covers (Layer 1) lack local cocharacter data, reflex fields
  and parahoric levels on the reductive-group carriers.
* Flatness of the standard GL and GSp chain models and closed polynomial Hodge
  and symplectic embeddings, including restriction of scalars
  and period-total embeddings (Layer 2), lack the polynomial models and represented
  lattice-chain Grassmannians.
* Canonical classical abelian-type local models and normalization of Hodge images
  (Layer 3) lack integral local-model v-sheaves and their scheme comparison morphisms.
* General minuscule weak normal representability (Layer 3) lacks those v-sheaves,
  kimberlites and the specialization-triple comparison.
* Root and Cartan tangent equalities for the Finkelberg–Mirkovic bound (Layer 4)
  lack algebraic affine Schubert schemes and their representation-bound subschemes.
* Formal-curve spanning of Schubert and reductive Weil-restriction special-fibre
  tangent spaces (Layer 4) lacks those schemes and the pointed formal-curve derivative
  interface; the existing Zariski tangent vector space alone is insufficient.
* Same-residue-field Schubert curves (Layer 5) lack companion partial affine flags,
  their valued-root orbit strata and the local-model comparison.
* EL/PEL chain torsors and the de Rham kernel comparison (Layer 6) lack integral
  polarized module-chain moduli and integral modification v-sheaves.
* The EL Drinfeld local-model isomorphism (Layer 6) lacks the represented determinant
  and Eisenstein models and their diamond comparison.
* The unitary Drinfeld local-model isomorphism (Layer 6) lacks these models with the
  signature cocharacter and the specified integral Hermitian lattice level.
* Connected geometric tubes for every bound (Layer 7) lacks local-model kimberlites,
  geometric tubes and the nearby-cycle sheaf categories.
* Normal minuscule scheme representability at every residue characteristic (Layer 7)
  lacks the local-model v-sheaf and its weakly normal scheme representative.
* Good embeddings for acceptable Hodge data and the admissible lattice criterion
  (Layer 7) lack the integral Hodge models, their map to a represented Grassmannian
  and the admissible-stratum comparison.
* Splitting-field inertia in the tame polynomial range, and the all-prime test-function
  theorem for every reductive group and dominant bound (Layer 8), lack local-model
  nearby cycles, central sheaves and parahoric Satake-parameter central functions.
  For minuscule bounds the latter theorem uses the normal scheme representative;
  for arbitrary bounds it uses the v-sheaf and its intersection complex.

-/

